        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "The Sentinels, as a group, are one hero. However, they are, individually, four hero [i]targets[/i]. If something affects the hero with the lowest hp and any one of the Sentinels fits that definition, then you can choose which one gets hit. If it says hero [i]target[/i], then it is the specific Sentinel with the lowest hp.\n\nThey count as one hero because then H isn&#39;t affected (just think, H would be four before anyone else has even chosen a hero, regardless of how many other players there actually were!). Also for stuff like Plague Rat - he flips when every hero is Infected, but only has five copies of Infection in his deck. So when it&#39;s the Sentinels&#39; turn to be Infected, you choose which individual one of the four will have the card attached to them.\n",
