        "raw": "[quote=\"robbritt\"]\n\nI read the thread on playing the Sentinels.&nbsp; I still need a little more clarification on damaging them.If a villain cards refers to damaging all hero targets, do all 4 Sentinels take damage?If it refers to &quot;highest HP/2nd lowest, etc.&quot;, do the individual Sentinels count towards that calculation?My guess is that both would be &quot;yes&quot;.&nbsp; I only aks because they if the answer is &quot;yes&quot;, then they are tissue paper in hurricane (at least in my two uses).&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\n\n[/quote]\n\nThey may look like tissue paper, but they have a ton of ways to heal, gain damage reduction, redirect damage away, and resurect even after being incaped. They also have a massive amount of effective health to chew through. While AoE affects them more than other heros, single target attacks are easily mitigated. Once the whole team (sentinels and the rest of the group) are around the same HP, there is a ton of ways to manipulate health to take advantage of the Sentinel&#39;s defensive tool kits and still lay down the damage.\n",
